# Fleet SSH access registry: the reviewed public keys that may open a session
# on a clan machine whose sshd reads only root-owned key files
# (modules/nixos/vps.nix renders /etc/ssh/authorized_keys.d/<user> from this
# file). Public material only; private keys live in the Bitwarden vault (see
# docs/git-keys.md).
#
# A key reaches a machine only through a reviewed commit here, exactly as a
# signing key becomes trusted only through a reviewed commit in
# modules/home/git/allowed-signers. Registration is access on those machines:
# a line added here can connect once the machine is redeployed, and a line
# removed cannot.
#
# One line per key, whitespace-separated:
#
#   NAME  KEYTYPE  BASE64-KEY
#
# NAME   stable identifier, written as the comment of the rendered
#        authorized_keys line.
# KEYTYPE/BASE64-KEY  the first two fields of the key's authorized_keys line.

